
title: Ed_Start_Day3
---

Eduard: Ah, Detective, what a pleasure.
Eduard: The boss has ordered us to start packing, but rest assured—no one has disturbed your precious crime scene.
Eduard: We’re drawing lots to decide who gets the unfortunate task of cleaning it up.
    -> You:  You might feel less grim about it knowing the culprit will be held accountable.
        Eduard: Will they, though?
        You: Of course. I'm here to erase the last traces of doubt.
    -> You: Is it fear that keeps you away, or mourning for your late friend?
        Eduard: If I'm honest, it's mostly the mess—always cluttered, then a murder scene, and now torn apart by an investigator.
        Eduard: But, well… murder scenes are rarely a pleasure to work in.
        You: I understand. And I’m here to clear away the last shreds of doubt.
Eduard: *smirks* Of course you are. Shall we begin, then? I assume you have more questions.
Eduard: Third time’s the charm.
<<jump Eduard_Questions_3>>

===
title: Eduard_Questions_3
---
<<declare $ed_clown_nose to false>>
<<declare $ed_torn_flyers to false>>
<<declare $ed_pocket_watch to false>>
<<declare $ed_pile_of_suits to false>>


    <<if $clown_nose is false and $crumpled_flyer is false and $pocket_watch is false>>
You: ... Actually, I have nothing as of now.
Eduard: Wow.
        <<jump Ed_Day3_End>>
    <<elseif $ed_clown_nose is false and $ed_torn_flyers is false and $ed_pocket_watch is false>>
You: *Open your notebook* let's see...
    <<elseif $ed_clown_nose is true xor $ed_torn_flyers is true xor $ed_pocket_watch is true>>
Eduard: Is there anything else? I don't have all day, you know.
    <<else>>
You: We're almost done, Eduard...
Eduard: You keep saying that.
    <<endif>>

-> You: \[pocket watch\] Is this one of the late Mr. Waddles' possessions? <<if $pocket_watch is true and $ed_pocket_watch is false>>
    <<jump Ed_Pocket_Watch>>
-> You: I assume Mr. Waddles took good care of his clothes, right? <<if $ed_pile_of_suits is false>>
    <<jump Ed_Pile_Of_Suits>>
-> You: \[torn flyer\] This has your name on it. <<if $crumpled_flyer is true and $ed_torn_flyers is false>>
    <<jump Ed_Torn_Flyers>>
-> You: \[clown nose] This doesn't seem like something Mr. Waddles would own. Is it yours? <<if $clown_nose is true and $ed_clown_nose is false>>
    <<jump Ed_Clown_Nose>>
-> You: Let us call it a day.
    <<jump Ed_Day3_End>>

    <<if ($clown_nose is false or $ed_clown_nose is true) and ($pocket_watch is false or $ed_pocket_watch is true) and ($clown_nose is false or $ed_clown_nose is true)>>  
