    <<endif>>  



===
title: Ed_Pocket_Watch
---
Eduard: ...
Eduard: *looks flushed beneath the pale makeup, pressing lips against another* No comment?
You: Was that a question?
Edaurd: I dont know. its just... *his gaze is fixed on the watch, as if watching a stray child*
    -> You: Look, if you're hiding something, I *will* find out. Some of your colleagues love to gossip.
        Eduard: They do, dont they?
    -> You: Alright. I’m filing this as evidence. You’ll never set eyes on it again...
        Eduard: *frustrated* Wait, no. Let’s not get ahead of ourselves.
Eduard: *signs* Okay, it’s mine. It is mine. Where did you find it, and... am I once again a suspect?
        -> You: In the crime scene. And yes.
            Eduard: Here we go again.
        -> You: In the crim scene, and no.
            Eduard: Not very helpful, though at least reassuring.
        -> You: In the crime scene, and maybe.
            Eduard: Mysterious, aren’t we?
Eduard: Very well. I lost it days ago—long before the incident.
Edaurd: I looked everywhere, turned every stone. Though, perhaps not everyone noticed me.
Eduard: I can be quite discreet about my business.
Eduard: Ah, our dear trumpet penguin... Quite the crow, was he not? Filling his nest with whatever shone and gleamed.
    -> You: So, you think he stole it?
        Eduard: A possession of mine found among his belongings? Yes. That that is called theft.
    -> You: Maybe someone planted it there...
        Eduard: *thinks* you suggest a scheme to make it appear as though I killed him to reclaim my watch?
        Eduard:  A bit dramatic, don’t you think?
Eduard: Poor little waddles couldn’t handle people having nice things, I suppose.
Eduard: I’m not like him. I don’t rub my belongings in other people’s faces.
You: Did you tell anyone your watch was missing?
Eduard: Not particularly. I tend to keep such matters to myself.
Eduard: I told maybe four... no, five people. Six if you count the deceased.
    -> You: Thats... *check notes* everyone.
        Eduard: *shrugs* They’re clowns. They all look the same to me.
    -> You: You’re very discreet.
        Eduard: *nods*
Eduard: Anyway... Can I have it back? I'm not the type to care much about material things...
Eduard: But this, this does hold some significance for me.
<<if $ed_pocket_mirror is true>>
Eduard: *smirks*  Even though I didn’t get it from my great-great-great-grandfather. 
<<endif>>
You:  I’m afraid not. I have to keep everything until I close the case.
    -> You:  You’ll get it back then, I promise.
        You: Unless, of course, you happen to be the killer.
    -> You: Even then, I cannot promise you will see it again.
        You: Not if you’re the killer, for instance.
Eduard:  Ah, to be caught and to lose the very object for which one committed murder.
Eduard: *winks* Now that, I would consider a fine jest for the stage.
Eduard: *His gaze lingers on the watch as you place it carefully into your suitcase, his eyes heavy with a trace of sorrow.*
    <<set $ed_pocket_watch to true>>
    <<jump Eduard_Questions_3>>
===
title: Ed_Pile_Of_Suits
---

Eduard: You'd be right to assume that, yes.
Eduard: One of his better qualities.
You:  I noticed his suits are sort of scattered in front of the rack.
Eduard:  Hm, it is indeed strange. He didn’t care about making a mess wherever he went,
Eduard:  But he was very careful about sorting his belongings.
Eduard:  He once asked the... you know... little one with the big hat? *gestures to show a big hat*
You: Teddy.
Edaurd: Was that his name?
Eduard: ... Asked that guy to head to his wagon and bring him his <i> Saturday hat</i>
Eduard: Then got mad that the wrong hat was brought to him.
Eduard: Fifteen minutes of this till he went to get the damn hat himself.
Eduard: *Pauses dramatically* They all looked the same. 
Eduard: He said the Saturday hat was precisely dusted for that day. 
Eduard: *Pauses* How dreadfully tedious as evidence. What else have you found? The murder weapon, perhaps? A letter brimming with vengeance?
Eduard: *Opens his arms theatrically* Another body?
You: Sorry to disappoint. 
        <<set $ed_pile_of_suits to true>>
        <<jump Eduard_Questions_3>>
===
title: Ed_Torn_Flyers
---
Eduard: *reaches his hand to get the flyer* Oh, yes. The now pretty much dead idea of our two-man show
Eduard: Though you must really look to see the name of the second man, yours truly.
Eduard: The dear, departed Waddles’ name, along with his trumpet and ego, have taken most of the page.
Eduard: *look at you* Pray, where did you come across it? We had not yet begun the distribution of these.
You: I found several torn and quite crumpled copies within the confines of the wagon.
    -> You: Was anyone else involved in this performance?
        Edaurd: No, it was solely the two of us. We have been rehearsing for quite some time, you see.
        Eduard: Waddles, in particular, was looking forward to it. *his expression turns wistful*
        You: You were not?
        Eduard:  Quite the contrary.. I was, indeed. It was, in all truth, a most serious, profound, and meaningful thing.
        Eduard: Unlike the majority of the shallow, trifling performances I am compelled to do as part of my job.
        Eduard: *sighs* We funded the flyers ourselves, from our own humble pockets. were all of them destroyed?
        You: That's all I found.
        Eduard: A shame. To think that such a humble flyer could trigger such fury in the hearts of some.
        Eduard: The people here, it seems, have no understanding of true art.
        Eduard: This, in and of itself, ought to be a crime. *he shakes the torn flyer with theatrical frustration.*
        -> You: Who else knew of your preparations for the performance??
            Eduard: *pauses to consider* We practiced in our spare time. Well, I did. Waddles didn't care much for rehearsals.
            Eduard: Unless, of course, it was past midnight.
            Eduard: I personally told no one, as far as I can remember.
            Eduard: *shrugs nonchalantly* 
                <<set $ed_torn_flyers to true>>
                <<jump Eduard_Questions_3>>
    -> You: Who else knew of your preparations for the performance??
            Eduard: *pauses to consider* We practiced in our spare time. Well, I did. Waddles didn't care much for rehearsals.
            Eduard: Unless, of course, it was past midnight.
            Eduard: I personally told no one, as far as I can remember.
            Eduard: *shrugs nonchalantly* I suppose someone may have been following me, or some such thing.
            -> You: Was anyone else involved in this performance?
                Edaurd: No, it was solely the two of us. We have been rehearsing for quite some time, you see.
                Eduard: Waddles, in particular, was looking forward to it. *his expression turns wistful*
