title: Ed_Clown_Nose
---

Eduard: It is not indeed. Though we did try to convince him.
Eduard: It is not mine, though.
You: Given the location where it was found, it could cast the owner in an unfortunate light, I dare say.
Eduard:  Yes, these things are quite tricky, as you might imagine.
Eduard: t’s no easy task removing it, you see. I’ve spent many a night battling with my trunk until I mastered the art of it...
Eduard: *Pauses abruptly* oh.
    -> You: You are aware of what that implies, are you not?
    -> You: Do you want me to tell you what it means?
Eduard: *coldly*  It could have fallen off the killer in the midst of a struggle, no doubt.
Eduard: And yet, I must remind you... it was found in the repair and storage wagon.
Eduard: It might have been placed there entirely unrelated to the tragedy.
    -> You: *say nothing*
    -> You: The place of its discovery strongly suggests it may have been rolling toward there.
        Eduard: It is a round object, after all. Round things have a tendency to roll.
    -> You: There are slight marks or impressions on it, likely from pressure applied.
        Eduard: More reasons for it to be simply left at the repair wagon.
Eduard: *swings his trunk anxiously*
Eduard:  I must admit, this is the first time I truly feel... uneasy. 
Eduard: And I cannot quite place why.
Eduard: But that nose is not mine.
Eduard: I should like to believe I am the sort of man who would remove his clown nose before committing such a heinous act.
You:  People often forget things in the heat of the moment.
Eduard: *Lifts his trunk, positioning it between the two of you* Hard to forget this, trust me.
Eduard: Also, I cannot be the only one cursed with such a peculiar part of a costume, can I?
Eduard: After all, this is a circus. Surely you can find another clown to accuse.
    -> You: Are you attempting to send me down a misguided path?
        Eduard: I’m merely reminding you that as a detective, you must consider every possibility.
    -> You:  Is this truly the full extent of your defense? Other clowns?
        Eduard: *gestures towards the clown nose*  Is this your entire case, then? One clown nose?
You: Dont worry.  I am taking all factors into account. As for the clown nose...
    -> You: It may indeed prove to be irrelevant in the grand scheme of things.
        Eduard: *nods* Quite so, I imagine.
        You: But just in case- Do you have another clown in mind?
        Eduard: *Shrugs*
        You: Can't think of any other clowns?
    -> You: I have another clown in mind, I confess.
        Eduard: oh. *looks relieved* Oh? Might I inquire who, pray tell?
    You: Teddy, your partner?
    Eduard: *looks confused* Teddy, my.. oh. Big hat?
    -> ‌You: big hat.
    -> You: You truly do not recall your own partner?
    Eduard: Truth be told, I try to forget being in this circus every day. Some things just end up slipping away first.
    Eduard: Yes, now that you mention it, the little one does wear a clown nose, doesn't he?
    Eduard: Come to think of it, I cannot say I have ever seen him without it.
    Eduard: *looks at you* Now, I am not in the business of casting aspersions, detective.
    Eduard: I still think that the nose is entirely irrelevant to this matter.
    Eduard: But, if you insist on making it central to the case... well, yes.
    Eduard: Then by all means, investigate another nose. Leave mine in peace.
You: Wouldn’t it be quite the irony if it were the very thing to undo you in the end?
Eduard: *Gestures dramatically* Indeed, detective. A fitting end for a clown’s career—brought low by a mere nose.
<<set $ed_clown_nose to true>>
<<jump Eduard_Questions_3>>

===

title: Ed_Day3_End
---
Eduard: Ah, so that settles it, does it?
You: Before we tie things up neatly, do you happen to know what little Teddy was up to at the time of the crime?
    Eduard: ...
    Eduard: ...
    You: *gesture your hands to illustrate someone small and round*
    Eduard: Ah, that fellow. No, I do not. And why should I?
    You: You... sort of share a wagon?
    Eduard: *Blinks* Do we?  I hadn't noticed him.
    Eduard: I'm afraid I can't help you with his whereabouts last night-or, for that matter, at any other time.
    You: *slowly nod and close you notebook*
Eduard: Wait... What happens now?
    -> You: You will know when the time is right. 
        You: After I report to your boss.
    -> You: I need to speak with the others.
        You: Then report to your boss. 
    Eduard: Report with a name, I assume?
    You: Hopefully.
    Eduard: So you haven't made up your mind?
    -> You: Hmm. No.
        You: You're suddenly very inquisitive.
    -> You: Hmm. Yes.
        You: You're suddenly very inquisitive.
Eduard: Naturally. Someone’s life—mine, perhaps—may be ruined if you misstep.
Eduard: Not to mention, a murderer would walk free. Lurking among us. 
Eduard: You're not saying more, are you?
Eduard:  I can only assume you don’t think it was me…
Eduard: Otherwise, you'd still be clawing for a confession.
    -> You: Or I’m gathering my witnesses and coming back for you.
        Eduard: Witnesses, now? This should be entertaining.
        Eduard: I'm relieved your're not building your case solely upon the random trinkets you pocketed.
        Eduard: I half expected to be interrogated over a misplaced carrot, given your methods.
        Eduard: But it won't come to a trial with witnesses... Boss will likely just shoot whoever you name. Less paperwork than an arrest.
        <<jump Ed_Day3_EndEnd>>
    -> You: Or my case is solid enough that I don’t need a confession.
        Eduard: Ah, yes. The grand deductions built upon the random trinkets you pocketed.
        Eduard: I half expected to be interrogated over a misplaced carrot, given your methods.
        Eduard: But it won't come to a confession... Boss will likely just shoot whoever you name. Less paperwork than an arrest.
        <<jump Ed_Day3_EndEnd>>
            
===
title: Ed_Day3_EndEnd
---

        -> You:  *Lie* But I truly don’t think you did it, Eduard.
        -> You:  *Mean it* But I truly don’t think you did it, Eduard.
    Eduard: *Amused smirk.* Truly? And why is that?
         -> You: You just dont have it in you. 
            Eduard: Unclear if that’s meant to flatter or offend.
         -> You: You would have done it differently.
            Eduard: What kind of murderer do you take me for?
            -> You: You’d have been less messy.
            -> You: You’d have been more brutal.
    Eduard: *Eyes set on you, nods*
    You: But really *tap on your notebook* because you were friends.
    Eduard: ...
    -> You: Enough to bring him books... <<if $eduard_russian_classic is true>>
    -> You: Enough to plan a two-man show <<if $ed_torn_flyers is true>>
    -> You: Enough to get emotional over a mirror... <<if $ed_pocket_mirror is true>>
    -> You: I can see your grief.
    Eduard: *Shifts uncomfortably.* Hmph. Perhaps.
    Eduard: He had a talent for burrowing under one’s skin.
    Eduard: His endless, pathetic attempts to seem grander than he was—exhausting.
    Eduard: And yet... I understood. He was just another trumpet penguin.
    Eduard: Step into Napoleon’s office, and you’ll see a thousand Waddles just like him, ready to take his place.
    Eduard: But he wanted more, you see.
    Eduard: He didn’t want to be just another trumpet penguin.
    You: *You eye him carefully*
    <<wait  2>>
    Eduard: *Pauses, then exhales.* Shame it was him who died, detective.
    Eduard: You would have loved interrogating him.
        -> You: Preferably I’d rather watch a circus perform than unravel a murder within one.
             Eduard: You know what's even better? Joining a circus! *opens his arms dramatically, his facial expression blank*
             Eduard: And I heard we just got one wagon free.
        -> You: The ones I’ve questioned have been… entertaining enough. Really.
             Eduard: You know what's even more entertaining? Joining a circus! *opens his arms dramatically, his facial expression blank*
             Eduard: And I heard we just got one wagon free.
===